## How to Ask Your Nail Tech for the Look You Want

Walking in and asking for **clown nails** with no further direction leaves too much open to interpretation, and most of the frustration around this trend traces back to exactly that gap. Name the register first: cute or creepy, then bring the specific reference.

Say "cute clown, primary colours, polka dots and a balloon accent" if that's your lane, or "Pennywise-inspired, white base, red detail, painted grin" if you're after the horror version specifically. Naming the shape matters too. Ask for almond or square if you want the design to hold clearly, and mention length if you're chasing the 3XL balloon effect. Bring one clear reference photo rather than five conflicting ones. Most nail techs who do Halloween sets have painted some version of this trend already this season, and a specific ask gets you a far closer result than a vague one ever will.

